# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Local dev database + env
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Every env variant, not just `.env`: pydantic-settings only reads `.env`, but the
# file a human creates by hand is as often `.env.local` or `.env.production`, and
# that one held real values while being tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local Claude Code working dir + ad-hoc scratch/working scripts
# (keep `git add -A` from sweeping local tooling into commits)
#
# `.claude/*` not `.claude/` on purpose: git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT
# directory is excluded, so ignoring the directory itself would make the negation
# below a no-op. The run-fpl-analyst driver is the documented offline way to
# exercise Layers 1-2 (root CLAUDE.md), so it belongs in the repo — a fresh clone
# without it cannot follow its own instructions. Local machine state
# (settings.local.json) stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.playwright-mcp/
check_squad.py
scratch/
scratch_*.py
*_scratch.py
